    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0010:0001",
      "source": "In this example, an asynchronous sequence called `Counter` produces `Int` values from `1` to `10`.",
      "ko": "`m * stride[4] + n * stride[5]`.",
      "sourceHash": "1f7626545a0e12ba857d2990fe6e1beeb09c6f119a2f26fafb7630bf9af5a6f3",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0010:0002",
      "source": "The `first(where:)` method returns the first member of the sequence that’s evenly divisible by both `2` and `3`.",
      "ko": "The `first(where:)` method returns the first member of the sequence that’s evenly divisible by both `2` and `3`.",
      "sourceHash": "55971f471597a6d8fd15f25e0dab515356b1b22495eef10cf9976f5045a4395b",
      "status": "failed"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:code:discussion:0011:0001",
      "source": "```swift\nlet divisibleBy2And3 = await Counter(howHigh: 10)\n    .first { $0 % 2 == 0 && $0 % 3 == 0 }\nprint(divisibleBy2And3 ?? \"none\")\n// Prints \"6\"\n```",
      "ko": "```swift\nlet divisibleBy2And3 = await Counter(howHigh: 10)\n    .first { $0 % 2 == 0 && $0 % 3 == 0 }\nprint(divisibleBy2And3 ?? \"none\")\n// Prints \"6\"\n```",
      "sourceHash": "a9c51493d9211db6b7c97b5fee398ebe74c66d51a50cb61904142c3bb66efe18",
      "status": "preserved"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0012:0001",
      "source": "The predicate executes each time the asynchronous sequence produces an element, until either the predicate finds a match or the sequence ends.",
      "ko": "The predicate executes each time the asynchronous sequence produces an element, until either the predicate finds a match or the sequence ends.",
      "sourceHash": "d2aa3335006e048e2d71aeb1bd5221aca914418231b108b41a4a9aae53994f0f",
      "status": "failed"
    },
